    "overview": "Compare the 1942 order that led to the incarceration of Japanese Americans with Congress's 1988 judgment of it.",
    "sources": [
      "executive-order-9066",
      "civil-liberties-act-1988"
    ],
    "sourcingQuestions": [
      "Executive Order 9066 never names any ethnic group. Why might it have been written that way, and what does that reveal about its purpose?",
      "The 1988 findings were written 46 years later, after a commission reviewed government records. What could Congress know in 1988 that the public did not know in 1942?"
    ],
    "subject": "history-social-studies",
    "template": "primary-source-analysis",
    "title": "A Grave Injustice"
  },
